<h3>Pharmino Academy · Terms of use and student agreement</h3>
<p>Version @Application.DTOs.Account.SignupTerms.Version · Effective date: [to be set] · Operated by [legal entity name], Commercial Registration [number], [address], Sultanate of Oman ("Pharmino", "we", "us"). Contact: [support email], [phone].</p>
<p>Please read these terms carefully. By creating an account you enter a binding electronic agreement with Pharmino, valid under the Electronic Transactions Law (Royal Decree 69/2008). If you don't agree, don't create an account.</p>

<h3>1. Who can register</h3>
<ol><li>You must be at least 18 years old and have full legal capacity to enter a contract.</li><li>The details you give us (name, email, date of birth, phone) must be true, complete and your own.</li><li>One person may hold only one account. Accounts are personal to the named student.</li></ol>

<h3>2. Your account</h3>
<ol><li>You are responsible for everything done through your account and for keeping your password and verification codes secret.</li><li>Your account may only be used by you, on your own devices. We limit how many devices and sessions can be active at once.</li><li>Tell us at once at [support email] if you think someone else has used your account.</li></ol>

<h3>3. Our content and your licence</h3>
<ol><li>All videos, PDFs, slides, notes, mock exams, questions, answers, explanations, audio, images and software on the platform ("Content") belong to Pharmino Academy or its licensors and are protected by the Copyright and Neighbouring Rights Law (Royal Decree 65/2008, as amended by Royal Decree 132/2008) and international treaties.</li><li>When you enrol, we give you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to view the Content online, through the platform only, for your own exam preparation, for your course's access period.</li><li>You get no ownership of any Content. Everything not expressly allowed is forbidden. The limited free uses in Article 20 of the Copyright Law do not cover sharing, copying or posting Content online.</li></ol>

<h3>4. What you must not do</h3>
<p>Without our written permission you must not, directly or through anyone else:</p>
<ol><li>share, send, upload, post, sell, rent or otherwise distribute any Content, in whole or in part, by any means, including Telegram, WhatsApp, Google Drive, social media, email, USB drives or printed copies;</li><li>download or try to download Content, including with download managers, browser extensions, scripts or by extracting stream or cache files;</li><li>record, film or photograph Content, including screen recording and filming the screen with another device;</li><li>take screenshots or copies of PDF pages, slides or questions;</li><li>remove, hide, crop, blur or change any watermark, forensic code or ownership notice (these are rights management information under Article 40 of the Copyright Law);</li><li>bypass, disable or interfere with any security or technical protection measure (Article 40 of the Copyright Law), or use bots, scrapers or automated tools;</li><li>share your account or let anyone else use it, or use the platform on behalf of a group;</li><li>sell, rent or transfer your account or enrolment;</li><li>reproduce, translate, adapt or teach from the Content in any course, class, group or commercial activity.</li></ol>

<h3>5. How we detect breaches</h3>
<p>Every video and PDF carries visible and hidden watermarks that identify the account it was shown to. We also record sign-ins, IP addresses, devices and viewing activity to protect the Content (see section 9). Leaked material can be traced to the account it came from.</p>

<h3 id="su-terms-6">6. Agreed compensation for breaches</h3>
