<p>Any breach of these terms may also lead to suspension or closure of your account without refund.</p>

<h3>8. Reporting to the authorities</h3>
<p>Copyright infringement for financial gain and circumventing technical protection are criminal offences under Article 52 of the Copyright Law (imprisonment of 3 months to 2 years and/or a fine of 2,000 to 10,000 OMR, doubled for repeat offences), and the Public Prosecution may act without a complaint (Article 49). Unauthorised access, fraud and impersonation online are offences under the Cybercrime Law (Royal Decree 61/2026). We may report suspected offences to the competent authorities. This is separate from, and in addition to, section 6.</p>

<h3>9. Your personal data</h3>
<p>We process your name, email, date of birth, phone number, IP address, device information and learning activity to create and run your account, deliver courses, prevent fraud and protect our Content, in line with the Personal Data Protection Law (Royal Decree 6/2022) and its Executive Regulations (Ministerial Decision 34/2024). We ask for your consent to this separately below. We don't sell your data. You can ask to see, correct or delete your data, or withdraw consent, at [privacy email]. Full details: Privacy Policy [link].</p>

